{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeHu5LH6kjwpWfmz7UST","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added H2 to `pom.xml` as a test-scoped dependency, so it's only on the test classpath. `mvn dependency:resolve` ran without errors.\n\n```xml\n<dependency>\n  <groupId>com.h2database</groupId>\n  <artifactId>h2</artifactId>\n  <version>2.5.252</version>\n  <scope>test</scope>\n</dependency>\n```\n\nI first tried version 2.3.232, but a pre-edit hook in your environment rejected it as outdated and asked for 2.5.252, so that's the version I used.\n\nTo use it in tests, connect with a JDBC URL like `jdbc:h2:mem:testdb;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1` (username `sa`, empty password). The `DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1` keeps the database alive between connections for as long as the test JVM runs.\n\nSeparately, your existing `junit` dependency has no `<scope>test</scope>`, so it gets bundled with your main code. You'll probably want to add that scope too. I didn't change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":16911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":194},"output_tokens":348,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bb51066-c4a7-44f5-9760-7795a0eb98c5","uuid":"4b6df52d-4299-44e2-a377-1dece7ff045a","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:39:04.308Z","request_id":"req_011CfeHu4wxRccgNJKKjKtRA"}
